From c64460a720370f328e823e47216f87597456607f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:52:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] SARP: compact formatter options

Adds nine formatter options that produce a denser code style, each defaulting
to the existing Black/PEP 8 behaviour so an unconfigured build is byte-identical
to upstream:

    annotation-spacing      x:int, ->bool
    top-level-blank-lines   one blank line between top-level defs
    operator-spacing        precedence-aware: a*b, a/b tight
    dict-spacing            {"a":1}
    slice-spacing           x[a():b()]
    nested-blank-lines      no blank lines between methods
    default-value-spacing   def f(x: int=1)
    import-trailing-comma   no trailing comma on wrapped imports
    comment-blank-lines     no blank lines around comments in nested scopes

All nine live in a self-contained `compact` module and are carried through
`PyFormatOptions` as a single `CompactOptions` field rather than nine
interleaved ones, so this patch touches upstream's own structs in one place
each. Call sites read `f.options().compact().<option>()`.
